#!/usr/bin/env etcs

# THE BROWSER'S BOOT SCRIPT: a window on the page's canvas, with its input pump
# already running by the time anyone can type.
#
# Handed to the runtime as argv[1] by index.html, so it runs BEFORE the
# navigator opens -- script mode and REPL mode are not alternatives in this
# binary, the script runs and then main falls through to the terminal
# (drive_main_loop_then_exit, core/CommandExecutor.h). That is the whole reason
# the pump can exist "on load" without anything new in C++: the boot path for a
# page is the boot path for a script, and it already ended in a prompt.
#
# NO `#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules`, and that is the one line every other script
# has. In the browser the providers are already bound before main() runs
# (ETCS::preload_web_modules, loaders/etcs.cc) from the .wasm files the page
# staged into MEMFS -- so there is no directory to import from and nothing left
# for an import to do. The names below resolve out of the catalog those loads
# already filled.

# The window IS the canvas. 1024x768 matches index.html's element; Create calls
# emscripten_set_canvas_element_size on "#canvas" with exactly these numbers
# (OS/GLFWWindow.h), so the element is resized to match rather than the reverse
# -- which is why the page can state a size in CSS and still get a correctly
# sized framebuffer.
spawn WindowProvider::Window main
main.Create(1024, 768, ETCS Web)

# THE SAME PUMP SCRIPT THE OS SIDE USES, unmodified and by name. Not a browser
# variant: window_events.etcs states `window.ProduceEvents() -> window.ConsumeEvents()`
# and detaches the pointer channel, and neither half knows what platform it is
# on -- a window is an InputSource either way, and the GLFW entry points that
# have to touch the DOM are marshalled to the main thread by glfw_web
# (OS/GLFWWindow.h) rather than being avoided here.
#
# DETACHED BECAUSE ProduceEvents BLOCKS. It is the OS message pump as well as
# the event source: a `while (IsActive())` loop around PollEvents, which on the
# page's own thread would stop the page. So it runs on its own thread and the
# navigator keeps the main one.
#
# AND A THREAD IS SAFE HERE BECAUSE OF WHERE THIS SCRIPT RUNS. What the browser
# cannot survive is a Worker starting while the main module is still inside
# loadDynamicLibrary -- the reason for the deferred static init and for
# etcs_boot_runtime_threads. This script is argv[1], so every module is already
# loaded and the pool is already armed by the time this line is read. The
# constraint was never "no threads", it was "not yet".
detach window_events.etcs window=main
